# Example P-code Patch File
# ==========================
#
# This file demonstrates the format for patching P-code at a specific address.
# Save as: ~/.ghidra_pcode_patches/<address>.pcode
# Example: ~/.ghidra_pcode_patches/00510456.pcode
#
# The address format must match Ghidra's display (no "0x" prefix typically).

# ============================================================================
# FORMAT
# ============================================================================
#
# OPCODE (output_varnode) = (input1), (input2), ...
#
# Varnode format: (space, offset, size)
#   - space: register, const, unique, ram, stack
#   - offset: hex (0x...) or decimal
#   - size: in bytes (decimal)

# ============================================================================
# x86 32-bit REGISTER OFFSETS
# ============================================================================
#
# EAX = 0x0     ECX = 0x4     EDX = 0x8     EBX = 0xc
# ESP = 0x10    EBP = 0x14    ESI = 0x18    EDI = 0x1c
#
# AL = 0x0 (size 1)    AH = 0x1 (size 1)    AX = 0x0 (size 2)
# CL = 0x4 (size 1)    CH = 0x5 (size 1)    CX = 0x4 (size 2)
# etc.

# ============================================================================
# COMMON PATTERNS
# ============================================================================

# --- Pattern 1: Fix ESP-relative load to EBP-relative ---
# Original: MOV EAX, [ESP+0x20c]   (ESP tracking lost -> BADSPACEBASE)
# Fixed:    MOV EAX, [EBP-0x8]     (correct frame-relative offset)
#
# INT_ADD (unique,0x10000,4) = (register,0x14,4), (const,0xfffffff8,4)
# LOAD (register,0x0,4) = (const,0x1b1,4), (unique,0x10000,4)

# --- Pattern 2: Fix ESP-relative store to EBP-relative ---
# Original: MOV [ESP+0x20c], EAX
# Fixed:    MOV [EBP-0x8], EAX
#
# INT_ADD (unique,0x10000,4) = (register,0x14,4), (const,0xfffffff8,4)
# STORE (const,0x1b1,4), (unique,0x10000,4), (register,0x0,4)

# --- Pattern 3: Simple register copy ---
# MOV EAX, EBP
#
# COPY (register,0x0,4) = (register,0x14,4)

# --- Pattern 4: Load immediate ---
# MOV EAX, 0x1234
#
# COPY (register,0x0,4) = (const,0x1234,4)

# --- Pattern 5: LEA with offset ---
# LEA EAX, [EBP-0x10]
#
# INT_ADD (register,0x0,4) = (register,0x14,4), (const,0xfffffff0,4)

# ============================================================================
# ACTUAL PATCH (uncomment and modify as needed)
# ============================================================================

# Example: Fix BADSPACEBASE at this instruction
# Step 1: Calculate EBP-relative address
INT_ADD (unique,0x10000,4) = (register,0x14,4), (const,0xfffffff8,4)

# Step 2: Load from that address into EAX
# Note: 0x1b1 is the space ID for RAM in Ghidra
LOAD (register,0x0,4) = (const,0x1b1,4), (unique,0x10000,4)

# ============================================================================
# NOTES
# ============================================================================
#
# 1. Space IDs vary by program. Check Ghidra's AddressFactory for your binary:
#    - ram/mem: Usually 0x1b1 for x86
#    - stack: Usually separate space
#
# 2. Unique space is for temporaries. Use high offsets (0x10000+) to avoid
#    conflicts with SLEIGH-generated unique varnodes.
#
# 3. The patch replaces ALL P-code for the instruction. You must provide
#    complete semantics, not just the part you want to change.
#
# 4. Test patches carefully - incorrect P-code can crash the decompiler
#    or produce nonsense output.
